<urn:atm:triage:finding/BA4-QA2-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BA4-QA2-003" ;
  triage:title "preflight_close signature deviates from the documented contract (stale-doc-read false positive)" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-2 (req-qa), PR #1408 @ 85da7db99, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1408#issuecomment-5643235732. req-qa reported the sprint doc specifies pub async fn preflight_close(reader: &dyn AsyncTaskLedgerReader, team: TeamName, task_id: &TaskId, deadline: ReadDeadline) -> Result<ClosePreflight, AtmError>, while the shipped function (crates/atm-core/src/task_close.rs) is pub fn preflight_close(rows: Vec<TaskRow>, task_id: &TaskId) -> ClosePreflight -- synchronous, no reader/team/deadline/Result. fenix's ruling (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1408#issuecomment-5643246196): REJECTED, stale read. At the PR head the sprint doc's Close section already records the shipped pure signature: pub fn preflight_close(rows: Vec<TaskRow>, task_id: &TaskId) -> ClosePreflight; with the note 'BA4-FIX-R1: CLI reads through daemon List; pure projection.' (sprint-BA.4 line 195-196), and no AsyncTaskLedgerReader/async fn preflight_close text remains anywhere in the doc. The exactness gate is met; req-qa read an older copy of the doc. No fix scheduled." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "requirements" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-core/src/task_close.rs (preflight_close), docs/plans/phase-ba/sprint-BA.4-atm-task-commands.md (Close section)" ;
  triage:status "dismissed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T03:50:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-12T03:50:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
